course: dictionary
lesson: 8901
title: Mild words and everyday meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Shucks!» is an old-fashioned American word. People say it instead of a rude word when something goes wrong, so it is a mild word for disappointment.
explain: Context helps again: «Shucks, I missed the bus!» The speaker sounds let down, and missing the bus is a small problem, so shucks must show disappointment.
explain: Shucks can also be a noun or a verb about food. A shuck is the husk or shell of corn, peas or nuts, and to shuck is to remove them. The spelling is the same, so read the sentence to see which job the word is doing.
explain: The phrase «aw shucks» can show that someone is shy or modest, not proud. When you meet a new word, ask what it is doing in the sentence, then check your meaning by swapping it in.
fact: Shucks is an interjection, a short word that shows a feeling, such as disappointment.
fact: «Shucks» means a mild word for disappointment or shyness, and it is old-fashioned and American.
fact: As a noun, «shuck» means the husk or shell of corn, peas or nuts.
fact: As a verb, «shuck» means to remove the husks or shells, as in «shuck corn».
fact: Two useful phrases are «aw shucks» and «shuck corn».
exercise: «Shucks, I missed the bus!» What does shucks show? | Hunger for lunch | *Disappointment | Great excitement and joy | Anger at the bus driver
exercise: Grandad says, «Aw shucks, thanks for the praise.» What does aw shucks suggest? | *A shy, modest feeling | A loud, rude shout | A cold winter morning | A sleepy yawn
exercise: «We shucked the corn for dinner.» What does shucked mean here? | Ate it raw without washing | Cooked it in boiling water | *Removed the husks | Painted it bright yellow
test: «Shucks!» is an old-fashioned word. Which statement is true? | It is a rude word from modern slang | It is a kind of bus | It is a type of corn | *It is American and old-fashioned
test: In «a pile of corn husks», what is a husk? | A bus driver | A loud noise | *The outer covering of corn | A shy person
exam: Which sentence uses shucks as a mild word for disappointment? | «The corn husks were piled high.» | «We shucked the peas.» | *«Shucks, I missed the bus!» | «Shuck the nuts before dinner.»
